- node_id: head_grouped_streaming
- base_node_id: root
- title: Prototype head-grouped streaming decode
- difficulty_1_to_5: 3
- description: Implement one fused online-attention kernel in which each program owns one sequence and a small group of query heads, reusing each gathered Kc/Kp row across that group.
- rationale: This directly attacks the likely dominant cost: repeated indirect cache reads across 16 heads. It also avoids logits storage and intermediate global-memory traffic while covering most batch and sequence-length combinations.

