- description: Implement a dedicated short-sequence kernel that owns all work for one sequence, keeps query and softmax state resident, and avoids chunk workspaces or cross-program reduction.
- expected_vs_baseline_factor: 28.00x
- rationale: At the minimum workload of only a few KV indices, fixed launch, indexing, and synchronization costs dominate; a compact sequence-owned path can minimize those costs and share cache rows across heads.

